# Vite loads .env.<mode> by build mode, so every mode file is the natural place a
# developer drops a browser-prefixed build variable while testing a deploy
# configuration -- and anything that lands beside it. This repository reads no such
# variable since plan 04.2-06, but the family stays ignored: the risk it guards against
# is a file appearing, not a variable being read. Keep the checked-in example.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Tool-generated worktrees and local agent state. `.claude/worktrees/` holds whole
# duplicate checkouts of this repository, so a routine `git add -A` would otherwise
# commit a second copy of the source tree plus a worktree `.git` pointer file.
.claude/

# Local GSD runtime and generated research cache
.gsd/
.planning/research/.cache/

# NARROWED by plan 04.2-06, in the same commit that removed what it named:
# `dist-approved-host-probe/` was the throwaway output of the provider-selected
# ingestion-host bundle probe, which was retired here. Its successor runs in the HAOO
# repository, whose own .gitignore keeps both probe entries. An ignore rule naming a
# directory nothing in this repository can produce is a comment describing machinery that
# is not here.
#
# `.reports/` STAYS, and its reason changed rather than disappearing. The generator that
# produced it (`scripts/generate-haoo-report.mjs` and the `report:haoo` npm script) moved
# to the HAOO repository in the same commit, so nothing here writes this directory any
# more -- but an existing local checkout still has one, and those files carry aggregate
# product business counts. They were never repository content and must not reach a
# published bundle or a review diff just because their producer left.
.reports/
